.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/postcss-nested Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "PostCSS Nested"
.PP

.PP
\fRPostCSS\fP plugin to unwrap nested rules closer to Sass syntax\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
\&.phone {
  &_title {
    width: 500px;
    @media (max\-width: 500px) {
      width: auto;
    }
    body\&.is_dark & {
      color: white;
    }
  }
  img {
    display: block;
  }
}

\&.title {
  font\-size: var(\-\-font);

  @at\-root html {
    \-\-font: 16px;
  }
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
will be processed to:

.PP
.PP
.nf
\&.phone_title {
  width: 500px;
}
@media (max\-width: 500px) {
  \&.phone_title {
    width: auto;
  }
}
body\&.is_dark \&.phone_title {
  color: white;
}
\&.phone img {
  display: block;
}

\&.title {
  font\-size: var(\-\-font);
}
html {
  \-\-font: 16px;
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
Related plugins:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Use \fR\fRpostcss-current-selector\fP\fP \fBafter\fP this plugin if you want to use current selector in properties or variables values\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Use \fR\fRpostcss-nested-ancestors\fP\fP \fBbefore\fP this plugin if you want to reference any ancestor element directly in your selectors with \fR^&\fP\&.
.PP

.PP
Alternatives:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
See also \fR\fRpostcss-nesting\fP\fP, which implements \fRCSSWG draft\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR\fRpostcss-nested-props\fP\fP for nested properties like \fRfont-size\fP\&.
.PP

